    "body": "I do not understand why it is apparently found better to *sometimes* present the full name of a character (`LEFT PARENTHESIS`, `RIGHT PARENTHESIS`), and *sometimes* present the character itself (`,`, `«`, `»`), even if they all provide the Unicode identifier (`U+0028`, `U+002C`, `U+0029`). This seems very likely to lead to misunderstanding, and to be perceived by the reader as in error. Issues are almost certain to arise when using wrappers such as braces `{}`, (square) brackets `[]`, and angle brackets `<>`, which names are often confused with each other or even displaced by another wrong name.\r\n```suggestion\r\nU+0029 RIGHT PARENTHESIS, and separating each variable name with U+002C (,). The number of variables\r\n```",
